WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.079
MIDI files explained, with a piano roll you can play.

2
00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:10.737
Why a MIDI file has no sound in it, what note numbers, velocity and channels

3
00:00:10.737 --> 00:00:15.285
mean, and how to play and render MIDI to MP3 or WAV in the browser.

4
00:00:16.685 --> 00:00:21.501
Sheet music for machines. MIDI, the Musical Instrument Digital Interface,

5
00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:26.251
was agreed by instrument makers in 1983 so that keyboards, drum machines

6
00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:30.275
and computers from different brands could talk to each other.

7
00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:34.620
Why the same file sounds different everywhere.

8
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.454
Since the file only says play a violin, the quality depends on the violin

9
00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:40.513
sound available.

10
00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:44.288
Playing and converting in OpenFile.

11
00:00:44.288 --> 00:00:49.024
MIDI Player and Converter opens .mid, .midi and .kar karaoke files.

12
00:00:50.324 --> 00:00:54.335
Going the other way. People sometimes ask for MP3 to MIDI.

13
00:00:55.635 --> 00:00:59.276
To try it, open MIDI Player and Converter in OpenFile.

14
00:00:59.276 --> 00:01:03.119
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:06.557
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:12.340
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
